== number of validation questions (no K) ==
L=  1e+01: certificate of a faithful run (gamma=0.1, delta=0.05): m = 300 = 300 h;  with tolerance theta=0.1: m = 300 = 300 h
L=  1e+03: certificate of a faithful run (gamma=0.1, delta=0.05): m = 3e+04 = 15 human-years;  with tolerance theta=0.1: m = 300 = 300 h
L=  1e+06: certificate of a faithful run (gamma=0.1, delta=0.05): m = 3e+07 = 1.5e+04 human-years;  with tolerance theta=0.1: m = 300 = 300 h

== many deployed runs (deterministic human) ==
Expected number of unfaithful calls in R deployed runs <= R L K ln2 / n.  With S = R L deployed calls:
  (questions n) x (expected unfaithful calls) <= S K ln2.
  K=1e+02, S=1e+06 calls: n = sqrt(S K ln2) = 8.33e+03 questions gives at most 8.33e+03 unfaithful calls (fraction of calls put to the human: 8.33e-03);  n = S/100 gives at most 6.93e+03 unfaithful calls
  K=1e+02, S=1e+09 calls: n = sqrt(S K ln2) = 2.63e+05 questions gives at most 2.63e+05 unfaithful calls (fraction of calls put to the human: 2.63e-04);  n = S/100 gives at most 6.93e+03 unfaithful calls
  K=1e+02, S=1e+12 calls: n = sqrt(S K ln2) = 8.33e+06 questions gives at most 8.33e+06 unfaithful calls (fraction of calls put to the human: 8.33e-06);  n = S/100 gives at most 6.93e+03 unfaithful calls
  K=1e+04, S=1e+06 calls: n = sqrt(S K ln2) = 8.33e+04 questions gives at most 8.33e+04 unfaithful calls (fraction of calls put to the human: 8.33e-02);  n = S/100 gives at most 6.93e+05 unfaithful calls
  K=1e+04, S=1e+09 calls: n = sqrt(S K ln2) = 2.63e+06 questions gives at most 2.63e+06 unfaithful calls (fraction of calls put to the human: 2.63e-03);  n = S/100 gives at most 6.93e+05 unfaithful calls
  K=1e+04, S=1e+12 calls: n = sqrt(S K ln2) = 8.33e+07 questions gives at most 8.33e+07 unfaithful calls (fraction of calls put to the human: 8.33e-05);  n = S/100 gives at most 6.93e+05 unfaithful calls
